# tor — Tor client (niri dotfiles)
# Human-readable reference. The live torrc is generated by NixOS from
# `services.tor.settings` in modules/nixos/services/tor.nix; keep this file in
# sync with that module. See docs/PRIVACY.md for usage.

# ── Client mode: run Tor, NOT as a relay or exit node ────────────────────────
ClientOnly 1

# ── SOCKS proxy for apps that route via Tor (proxychains/torsocks) ───────────
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050

# ── Control port for `nyx` / torctl ──────────────────────────────────────────
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
CookieAuthentication 1

# ── DNS over Tor (optional; keep OFF unless you route ALL DNS via Tor) ───────
# DNSPort 127.0.0.1:5353
# AutomapHostsOnResolve 1
# AutomapHostsSuffixes .onion,.exit

# ── Logging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Log notice file /var/log/tor/notices.log

# ── Usage: route a single command through Tor ─────────────────────────────────
#   torsocks curl https://check.torproject.org/
#   torsocks ssh -o ProxyCommand='torsocks nc %h %p' user@host
